Job Responsibilities / Description:
Job Context
Smart, innovative, and energetic persons are invited to apply for the
Assistant Project Electrical Engineer
position in a running project.
Job Responsibilities:
To assist the superior in all designs, dra/;wings and specifications according to the project Standards;
To supervise, monitor and ensure overall quality of construction works including finishing works and the quality of materials being used at respective projects as per the specifications under the PEE;
To be responsible for preparing work plans and periodical reports for on-going projects under the supervision of PEE;
To be responsible for solving any construction-related problems in consultation with the consultants, if necessary, that arise at the project sites;
To be responsible for liaising with Own Head Office, other professionals within design teams (consultants) and contractors' representatives during construction;
To be responsible for the preparation of Engineering Documents and other documental works for the construction of on-going projects and maintain the same;
To be responsible for attending meetings and competently communicate with Head Office, Contractors and major asset owners and stakeholders as per requirements;
To be responsible for managing, directing and monitoring progress during each phase of a project;
To be responsible for taking measurements of the finished works for running bills and recording those in MBs (Measurement Books);
To be responsible for checking the final MBs for final payment and refund security deposit with the commendation;
To be responsible for preparing the drawings with specifications and BoQ for special items of renovation works;
To have to be computer-literate and conversant with MS Office suite and relevant engineering software packages;
To have to be fluent in writing technical reports, e-mailing and internet browsing;
To have to assume any other responsibility and maintain any other register as assigned by the management.
To be responsible for any tangible or intangible loss or damage caused to the property or interest of the employing organization due to your negligence of duty, unprofessional activity or moral turpitude.

Experience:
At least 1 year
The applicants should have experience in the following business area(s): University
Freshers are also encouraged to apply.

Education Requirements:
Diploma in Electrical Engineering

Additional Requirements:
Age 22 to 35 years
Comprehensive knowledge in drawing development (2D and 3D in AutoCAD is a must, proficiency in written and oral communication in English, good technical skills.
Shall be responsible for Electrical and Information Technology activities.
It is mandatory to submit your original certificates (i.e: Diploma, SSC) and experience certificate to get the job.

Location:
Chattogram

Salary & Benefits:
Negotiable

Job Responsibilities / Description:
Company Overview:
China Harbour Engineering Company Ltd. (CHEC) is a leading Chinese state-owned international contractor, specialized in Road and Highway construction, Marine Engineering, Dredging, Ports and Harbours, Airports, Power Plants, and other large-scale infrastructure and civil works. CHEC operates through more than 154 branches (subsidiaries) worldwide, with business covering 100 countries and regions, including Bangladesh, employing more than 15,000 professionals worldwide. The company manages projects valued at over USD 20 billion, with an annual turnover exceeding USD 9 billion. CHEC is a global leader in large-scale infrastructure development with over 45 years of proven experience in delivering complex engineering projects. Its core expertise includes ports and harbour development, marine structures, capital and maintenance dredging, mass rapid transit (MRT) systems, roads and bridges, railways, airports, and industrial plant construction. The company is committed to providing comprehensive, end-to-end solutions to its clients. Leveraging its extensive international engineering experience, global business network, highly skilled management team, and strong financial capacity, CHEC delivers a wide range of project delivery models, including Design & Build (D&B), Engineering, Procurement and Construction (EPC), Project Management Consultancy (PMC), Build-Transfer (BT) and Build-Operate-Transfer (BOT).
Job Responsibilities
:
Prepare documentation in Chinese and operate relevant Chinese software as required;
Review and analyze tender and bidding documents;
Prepare summaries of tender requirements and qualification criteria;
Perform quantity take-offs from drawings and prepare comparison sheets;
Assist in estimating direct and indirect project costs;
Prepare RFQs and coordinate with suppliers and subcontractors;
Collect and analyze material and construction cost data from local and international sources;
Support market research on ongoing and upcoming projects;
Maintain and update material and cost databases.

Experience:
2 to 4 years
The applicants should have experience in the following business area(s): Engineering Firms, Multinational Companies

Education Requirements:
Bachelor of Science (BSc) in Civil Engineering
Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering/Marine Engineering from a reputed University;

Additional Requirements:
Graduates from Chinese universities will be given preference;
Minimum two (02) years of relevant professional experience;
Must be proficient in both Chinese and English languages (verbal and written);
Strong knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint;
High level of attention to detail and accuracy;
Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team.

Skills Required:
Chinese Language, Microsoft Office

Location:
Dhaka

Salary & Benefits:
Negotiable

QUALIFICATIONS:

 Graduate of a 4-year (degree) course in Computer Science, Computer Engineer or any IT related courses.

Minimum of 2–3 years of professional experience in software development, with at least 1 year specifically focused on the Zoho platform.

Proven track record of deploying low-code/no-code solutions that integrate with traditional custom-coded backends.

Strong analytical skills with the ability to translate complex business workflows into technical requirements.




Key skills:

a.      Mastery of Deluge Scripting, Zoho CRM Blueprints, Zoho Creator Form/Report Actions.

b.     Proficiency in JavaScript (for Widgets), and familiarity with Node.js or Python.

c.      Strong understanding of RESTful APIs, JSON, and Webhook handling.

d.     Solid knowledge of Relational Databases (RDBMS) and SQL logic.

e.      Experience with Figma (for UI prototyping) and project management tools like ClickUp/Jira.

f.      API & Webhook Integration




Minimum Requirements:

Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related IT field.

At least 2 years of relevant experience in software development.

Proficient in Programming, HTML, JavaScript, Bootstrap, PHP, and SQL.




Essential Job Functions:

1.              Design, Coding, Testing, Documentation in the areas of Development and Maintenance;

2.              Write complex Deluge scripts for automation, custom functions, and scheduled tasks;

3.              Develop and maintain REST API integrations and Webhooks between Zoho and external tech stacks (e.g., Node.js/Python backends, AWS, and SMS Gateways);

4.              Design and optimize database schemas within Zoho Creator, ensuring data integrity, proper lookup relationships, and efficient performance for high-concurrency scenarios;

5.              Create intuitive user interfaces using Zoho’s Page Builder and develop custom Widgets using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript where necessary;

6.              Develops at all levels of the stack, from database to UI and everything in-between;

7.              Administer user roles, profiles, and permissions, including the management of Super Admin access for internal IT personnel;

8.              Maintain clear documentation of system architecture, Deluge scripts, and API endpoints to ensure team-wide clarity and future scalability;

9.              Production of accurate, unambiguous technical design specifications to the required level of detail in the timescales as defined by the Automation Manager;

10.           Production, preparation and execution of unit test plans;

11.           Testing the product in controlled, real situations before going live;

12.           Production of efficient and fully documented code;

13.           Production of supporting technical and installation documentation for internal publication;

14.           Achievement of agreed productivity targets in order to ensure developments are delivered within budget, to schedule and to defined quality standards;

15.           Completion of all necessary software and non-software components in the timescales as defined by the Project Manager;

16.           Works with little day to day supervision from immediate head;

17.           Tech Specs, Code and/or Unit Test Plans produced are all in line with the functional Specification;

18.           Ensures all work is reviewed to ensure adherence to the relevant development standards;

19.           Peer review and sign-off of others work;

20.           Timely and accurate reporting of project status as required by supervisor;

21.           Production and revision of accurate detailed estimates;

22.           Escalate product issues and suggest product improvements;

23.           Escalate all issues in a timely fashion;

24.           Maintaining the systems once they are up and running;

Coherent Solutions is a digital product engineering company focused on empowering business success. Our global team of 1700+ talented professionals collaborate seamlessly to deliver innovative solutions that drive measurable business impact. Headquartered in Minneapolis, USA, the company’s core competencies across 10 locations worldwide include product software development, IT consulting, data and analytics, machine learning, mobile app development, DevOps, Salesforce, and more.




We grow a team of advisors, not just order takers, and strive to make the company a place for career growth and opportunities. If you want to grow your core competencies, share your passion and be sure that every contribution is evaluated, we are on the same page.




Company Background

Our client is a leading life insurance company, part of a global financial services group. The company offers a wide range of products, including annuities and life insurance, delivered through a large nationwide network of agents.




Project Description

The project involves a production system for managing clients and the life insurance programs in which they are enrolled. The Azure DevOps Engineer will support the Azure-based platform behind the system, enabling secure, automated, and reliable delivery across application and data services.




Technologies

Azure, Terraform, Azure Key Vault
Azure DevOps, Argo CD, GitOps, SonarQube
Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), Docker, Kubernetes, Helm
Databricks, Unity Catalog
Azure Monitor, Application Insights, Log Analytics, PowerShell, Bash, Python




What You'll Do

Design, provision, and maintain scalable Azure infrastructure using Terraform, with a focus on modularity, reusability, security, and version control;
Build, optimize, and support YAML-based Azure DevOps CI/CD pipelines for infrastructure, application, containerized, and data workloads;
Implement and maintain GitOps deployment workflows using Argo CD for reliable application delivery to AKS clusters;
Embed DevSecOps practices into pipelines, including SonarQube integration, code quality checks, vulnerability scanning, secrets management, and compliance validation;
Administer and optimize Azure services, including VNets, Load Balancers, App Services, Key Vault, Storage Accounts, and Azure AD, following RBAC and governance best practices;
Configure monitoring and observability using Azure Monitor, Application Insights, and Log Analytics, and troubleshoot build, deployment, and performance issues;
Manage Azure Databricks workspaces, clusters, access controls, and Unity Catalog configurations, while automating Databricks deployments through Terraform and CI/CD workflows;
Collaborate with architecture, data engineering, and security teams; maintain technical documentation and runbooks; and mentor junior engineers on DevOps best practices;




Job Requirements

5+ years of experience in Azure DevOps, cloud automation, or similar roles;
Strong hands-on experience with Terraform, including modules, workspaces, backends, and state management;
Proven experience building and maintaining Azure DevOps Pipelines using YAML;
Hands-on experience with Argo CD and GitOps-based deployments to AKS;
Solid Azure administration skills, including RBAC, networking, storage, and cost governance;
Experience managing Databricks workspaces and clusters;
Experience integrating SonarQube into CI/CD pipelines for code quality assurance;
Hands-on experience with Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm;
Scripting proficiency in PowerShell, Bash, or Python;
Strong problem-solving skills, ability to work independently, and effective collaboration in cross-functional team;
English proficiency at Upper-Intermediate (B2) level or higher;
Availability to work the primary support shift from 4:00 PM to 12:00 AM CST, with attendance at 9:00 AM CST morning meetings as needed to ensure team overlap;




Nice to Have

Relevant certifications, such as Microsoft Certified (Azure DevOps Engineer, Azure Administrator Associate), HashiCorp Certified (Terraform Associate), or Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA);
Experience with Azure Bicep, ARM Templates, or Ansible;
Exposure to Azure Data Factory and Azure Synapse CI/CD automation;




What Do We Offer

The global benefits package includes:

Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;
Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;
Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;
Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;
Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;
Referral program for bringing in new talent;
Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.




If this opportunity excites you, send us your resume!

Please, note, that we will consider all the applications with due respect, but only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.




